From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:35:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: yield-os/wait-os time their traps at CNTFRQ_EL0, not
 24 MHz

0085 took a trap under 48 generic-timer ticks as short, 2 us at the
24 MHz an M1's timer runs at, and ntdll's sampler turned the ticks into
milliseconds at mach_absolute_time's 24 MHz. On the PLA-462 phone
(iPhone18,4) the timer runs about 42 times faster, consistent with the
1 GHz Armv8.6 fixes: The Witcher 3's [xp-pause] showed a thread 13 s
inside its traps in a 0.3 s tick, a wait-os:128:200 trap 14.5 ms
rather than at least 0.2 ms, and no trap ever short (48 ticks being
48 ns there).

ProcessInit now reads CNTFRQ_EL0 and sets IosPauseShortTicks to 2 us
of it, clamped to 1..4095 for the SUB's immediate
(FEX::Ios::PauseShortTicks), which the emitter takes as an argument;
"FEX: pause mode=" logs short-ticks= and cntfrq=. madeira-unix 0223
converts at CNTFRQ_EL0 the same way.

Linear: PLA-462
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-29-fex-pause-yield-os.md, tools/tests/test_fex_pause_yield_os.py
Offered-upstream: no; the switch is Playport's iOS host's
